        "query_signature": "Causal policies must satisfy $(\\epsilon_{\\mathrm{priv}},\\delta_{\\mathrm{priv}})$ joint differential privacy. Inputs $T,d,\\mathcal A,\\phi,\\epsilon_{\\mathrm{priv}},\\delta_{\\mathrm{priv}}$ are public; the context distribution $P$, reward parameter $\\theta_\\star$, and positive gap $\\Delta_{\\min}$ are hidden. Received feedback may be stored and reused computationally. No unrevealed historical information or extra queries to exhausted samples are available; any within-round full-function or common-sample access must be explicit.",
        "response_signature": {
          "feedback": "context before action and played reward after action"
